271
00:17:17,160 --> 00:17:18,160
Are you okay with me…

272
00:17:19,319 --> 00:17:24,160
getting close to Dean?

273
00:17:27,560 --> 00:17:28,200
Mm-hmm.

274
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:30,280
Why wouldn’t I be?

275
00:17:32,360 --> 00:17:36,560
You’re not planning to
get serious with him anyway, right?

276
00:17:43,520 --> 00:17:44,000
Yeah.

277
00:17:46,560 --> 00:17:48,280
I’m gonna hang up now.
I’ve got something to draw.

278
00:18:18,240 --> 00:18:21,080
[TRY SPENDING ALONE TIME
ON AN IMPORTANT DAY.]

279
00:18:21,080 --> 00:18:24,320
[YOU’LL KNOW IT’S ONLY YOU WHO
ARE TRULY IMPORTANT TO YOURSELF.]

280
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:38,600
[TRY SPENDING ALONE TIME
ON AN IMPORTANT DAY.]

281
00:18:38,800 --> 00:18:42,320
[I KNOW YOU HATE GETTING
BD WISHES ON YOUR ACTUAL BD,]

282
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:45,520
[BUT PLEASE MAKE
AN EXCEPTION FOR ME.]

283
00:19:20,560 --> 00:19:21,160
(Are you free?)

284
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:22,680
I’m not.

285
00:19:42,240 --> 00:19:43,640
Hey, what’s up?

286
00:19:44,200 --> 00:19:45,080
You said you weren’t free.

287
00:19:46,280 --> 00:19:47,160
Guess I gave in to my heart.

288
00:19:50,280 --> 00:19:50,840
Okay.

289
00:19:51,800 --> 00:19:52,960
Here are the rules.

290
00:19:53,360 --> 00:19:55,040
We only talk when we feel like it.

291
00:19:55,440 --> 00:19:57,000
We only meet when we feel like it.

292
00:19:58,400 --> 00:20:00,960
But I promise that every time we meet,

293
00:20:01,760 --> 00:20:04,520
I’ll make it clear
how long we’re spending together.

294
00:20:06,600 --> 00:20:07,760
I won’t ditch you halfway through again.

295
00:20:10,080 --> 00:20:10,720
Good.

296
00:20:11,920 --> 00:20:13,040
That’s fairer.

297
00:20:14,960 --> 00:20:17,160
So, what do you want to do today?

298
00:20:20,440 --> 00:20:21,640
Didn’t you say you wanted to hit on me?

299
00:20:22,880 --> 00:20:23,520
Go ahead.

300
00:20:25,240 --> 00:20:26,200
I’m right here. Hit on me.

301
00:20:28,680 --> 00:20:31,200
Does that mean this is a date?

302
00:20:37,680 --> 00:20:38,280
Mhm.

303
00:20:55,640 --> 00:20:57,080
[SHARE LOTS OF PHOTOS.]

304
00:20:57,080 --> 00:20:59,280
[GIVE DR. PUN
MORE CHANCES TO SEE THEM.]

305
00:20:59,560 --> 00:21:00,880
[SHARE LOTS OF PHOTOS.]

306
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:02,280
[GIVE DR. PUN
MORE CHANCES TO SEE THEM.]

307
00:21:03,280 --> 00:21:05,200
[DON’T JUST BARK ORDERS.]

308
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:07,360
[YOU NEED TO START
MAKING A MOVE YOURSELF.]

309
00:21:21,440 --> 00:21:25,040
Did I miss him so much
I’m hallucinating his face?

310
00:21:30,680 --> 00:21:31,960
hit! He’s real.

311
00:21:31,960 --> 00:21:32,760
Dr. Pun!

312
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:34,200
Hello!

313
00:21:35,720 --> 00:21:36,680
Hi, Ten.

314
00:21:38,760 --> 00:21:39,760
Hi, there.

315
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:41,000
Hi.

316
00:21:44,400 --> 00:21:45,560
Do you live around here?

317
00:21:47,280 --> 00:21:48,000
No, I don’t.

318
00:21:48,240 --> 00:21:51,160
It’s close to your clinic, so I come here.

319
00:21:53,880 --> 00:21:55,120
I mean…

320
00:21:56,000 --> 00:22:01,240
If anything happens to Mademoiselle,
I can get her to you quickly.

321
00:22:01,880 --> 00:22:02,680
Ah.

322
00:22:04,240 --> 00:22:07,400
I really had no idea you jogged here.

323
00:22:08,600 --> 00:22:11,520
I never ran into you here.
I was almost ready to give up.

324
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:14,280
I mean…

325
00:22:15,640 --> 00:22:18,080
You must get off work late.

326
00:22:18,520 --> 00:22:19,880
You probably don’t
have much time to exercise.

327
00:22:20,760 --> 00:22:21,280
Right?

328
00:22:22,360 --> 00:22:24,760
I usually play badminton with Moth.

329
00:22:25,920 --> 00:22:28,680
But today’s Moth’s birthday,
so he spends the day by himself.

330
00:22:30,680 --> 00:22:32,320
Don’t look so surprised.

331
00:22:32,760 --> 00:22:34,000
Moth’s just weird like that.

332
00:22:34,760 --> 00:22:37,840
Every year, he spends his birthday alone.

333
00:22:39,320 --> 00:22:42,800
I thought Moth was with Dean.

334
00:22:49,080 --> 00:22:49,760
Excuse me?

335
00:22:50,440 --> 00:22:55,280
I saw it on Dean’s Stories.
He’s with Moth.

336
00:23:03,880 --> 00:23:05,800
Will you excuse me? I’m gonna go run now.

337
00:23:12,760 --> 00:23:14,720
(You need to start making a move yourself.)

338
00:23:16,280 --> 00:23:17,480
Can I run with you?

339
00:23:19,640 --> 00:23:21,000
Hey. Dr. Pun!

340
00:23:21,920 --> 00:23:23,080
Dr. Pun. Wait for me!

341
00:23:24,160 --> 00:23:24,920
Let’s go, baby.

342
00:23:25,560 --> 00:23:27,360
Oh, you’re pretty heavy.

343
00:23:29,040 --> 00:23:29,840
Dr. Pun!

344
00:23:31,600 --> 00:23:32,560
Dr. Pun!

345
00:23:38,960 --> 00:23:40,640
This is what you want to do?

346
00:23:42,600 --> 00:23:44,520
I usually work out on this day of the week.

347
00:23:46,640 --> 00:23:46,960
Why?

348
00:23:48,400 --> 00:23:48,960
Afraid you’ll wear yourself out?

349
00:23:51,720 --> 00:23:54,040
You’re the one who’s afraid of
wearing yourself out.

350
00:23:54,480 --> 00:23:55,240
Please.

351
00:23:55,960 --> 00:23:57,080
I used to be an athlete.

352
00:23:57,440 --> 00:23:57,800
Huh?

353
00:23:59,240 --> 00:24:02,280
So you’re an athlete and an artist?

354
00:24:02,640 --> 00:24:03,840
I’m an all-rounder.

355
00:24:04,240 --> 00:24:05,880
What sport did you play?

356
00:24:08,640 --> 00:24:09,600
Club-and-sword dancing?

357
00:26:20,920 --> 00:26:21,280
Here.

358
00:26:25,720 --> 00:26:26,320
Aren’t you tired at all?

359
00:26:30,640 --> 00:26:32,560
You’re a former athlete, after all.

360
00:26:38,200 --> 00:26:39,040
Why are you smiling?

361
00:26:39,040 --> 00:26:40,160
Can’t you see me sweating?

362
00:26:43,880 --> 00:26:44,600
Look at my heart rate.

363
00:26:46,040 --> 00:26:47,360
Do you still have to ask whether I’m tired?

364
00:26:48,080 --> 00:26:50,160
Then you’re really good at hiding it.

365
00:26:51,240 --> 00:26:52,480
I can’t even tell you’re tired.

366
00:26:54,320 --> 00:26:57,920
Did you lie about being a former athlete?

367
00:26:58,080 --> 00:27:01,080
I didn’t. I really was.

368
00:27:03,200 --> 00:27:05,120
I played pétanque.

369
00:27:09,600 --> 00:27:11,200
What else was I supposed to play?

370
00:27:12,440 --> 00:27:13,920
I was sick all the time as a kid.

371
00:27:14,520 --> 00:27:15,800
I had the flu almost every week.

372
00:27:17,040 --> 00:27:18,040
I’d faint whenever I was out in the sun.

373
00:27:18,960 --> 00:27:20,240
When it rained,
my allergies would get worse.

374
00:27:21,040 --> 00:27:24,000
But you look healthier now.

375
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:27,080
Look at you. You’ve even got biceps.

376
00:27:29,680 --> 00:27:30,520
Because I’m all grown up now.

377
00:27:32,480 --> 00:27:35,520
Whatever your weakness is,
you have to work on it.

378
00:27:46,040 --> 00:27:46,880
Why are you taking pictures of me?

379
00:27:47,680 --> 00:27:49,320
You hardly ever smile.

380
00:27:50,080 --> 00:27:50,680
You’re exaggerating.

381
00:27:51,520 --> 00:27:52,400
I smile all the time.

382
00:27:53,120 --> 00:27:53,960
All the time?

383
00:27:54,960 --> 00:27:56,960
Your smiles don’t even add up
to ten seconds a day.

384
00:28:01,920 --> 00:28:02,280
All right.

385
00:28:03,000 --> 00:28:04,240
I picked the first activity.

386
00:28:05,840 --> 00:28:06,920
Now it’s your turn to pick the next one.

387
00:28:08,720 --> 00:28:09,440
What do you want to do?

388
00:28:33,200 --> 00:28:34,200
This is what you came up with?

389
00:28:35,200 --> 00:28:36,480
The best your brain could do?

390
00:28:37,280 --> 00:28:37,720
Why?

391
00:28:38,600 --> 00:28:39,320
It’s a classic.

392
00:28:47,960 --> 00:28:48,440
My treat.

393
00:28:57,520 --> 00:28:58,440
You said this was a date.

394
00:28:59,360 --> 00:28:59,960
Smile.

395
00:29:01,920 --> 00:29:02,840
Do I have to smile on dates?

396
00:29:05,120 --> 00:29:06,960
You do, when taking pictures.

397
00:30:07,040 --> 00:30:07,440
Here.

398
00:30:11,960 --> 00:30:12,640
Keep it.

399
00:30:13,160 --> 00:30:13,800
I don’t want it.

400
00:30:14,720 --> 00:30:15,920
We each get one.

401
00:30:16,760 --> 00:30:18,280
Come on. Take it.

402
00:30:23,840 --> 00:30:25,120
What do you want to do next?

403
00:30:26,320 --> 00:30:29,200
Um… I can’t think of anything.

404
00:30:31,640 --> 00:30:32,400
Should we call it a day?

405
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:40,200
Who was it that said he’d
make time for me whenever we hung out?

406
00:30:41,720 --> 00:30:43,400
We’ve been together for six hours.

407
00:30:44,280 --> 00:30:45,200
Isn’t that enough?

408
00:30:56,400 --> 00:30:57,680
My friend asked if I wanted to
go to the same club.

409
00:30:59,160 --> 00:30:59,800
Is that really a friend?

410
00:31:01,440 --> 00:31:01,920
Yes.

411
00:31:03,080 --> 00:31:03,600
A friend.

412
00:31:06,240 --> 00:31:06,840
Why?

413
00:31:09,040 --> 00:31:09,760
Are you jealous?

414
00:31:10,680 --> 00:31:11,120
No.

415
00:31:12,880 --> 00:31:14,440
Go with whoever invited you.

416
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:16,760
We can split up here.

417
00:31:17,520 --> 00:31:18,080
Bye.

418
00:31:20,360 --> 00:31:21,240
Isn’t it your birthday today?

419
00:31:26,920 --> 00:31:27,480
How did you know?

420
00:31:28,440 --> 00:31:29,360
Because I pay attention.

421
00:31:31,280 --> 00:31:33,320
When you make a new friend,
don’t you look up their birthday?

422
00:31:35,160 --> 00:31:35,720
No.

423
00:31:36,640 --> 00:31:37,560
So, what now?

424
00:31:39,200 --> 00:31:40,280
It’s your birthday.

425
00:31:41,760 --> 00:31:43,280
Don’t rush home to be alone.

426
00:31:45,160 --> 00:31:45,800
That’s depressing.

427
00:31:47,240 --> 00:31:47,680
Why?

428
00:31:49,160 --> 00:31:50,520
Can’t I spend my birthday with myself?

429
00:31:52,400 --> 00:31:53,120
Tell you what,

430
00:31:53,880 --> 00:31:55,800
I’ve spent more than ten birthdays by myself,

431
00:31:56,640 --> 00:31:57,600
and I’m still alive.

432
00:31:59,040 --> 00:31:59,400
Yeah?

433
00:31:59,760 --> 00:32:00,200
Mm-hmm.

434
00:32:01,760 --> 00:32:05,880
Then why did you come out
to spend time with me today?

435
00:32:09,400 --> 00:32:10,480
You were lonely, weren’t you?

436
00:32:14,160 --> 00:32:15,040
It’s up to you, then.

437
00:32:16,080 --> 00:32:20,600
If you want to go back to your tiny,
quiet room and spend your birthday alone,

438
00:32:22,520 --> 00:32:23,320
that’s your choice.

439
00:32:25,360 --> 00:32:26,800
Who said I was going back to my place?

440
00:32:47,120 --> 00:32:49,480
So you booked a table
on a boat just to eat alone?

441
00:32:50,840 --> 00:32:51,840
You’re crazy.

442
00:32:53,080 --> 00:32:53,800
How’s that crazy?

443
00:32:54,680 --> 00:32:57,520
It’s my birthday. I can do whatever I want.

444
00:32:58,680 --> 00:32:59,000
But…

445
00:33:00,240 --> 00:33:00,960
Does it even feel right?

446
00:33:04,720 --> 00:33:07,600
If you won’t stop judging me,
jump overboard and swim home.

447
00:33:07,600 --> 00:33:08,280
Okay, okay.

448
00:33:08,560 --> 00:33:09,120
I’ll stop.

449
00:33:13,760 --> 00:33:16,000
Good thing I followed you here.

450
00:33:16,600 --> 00:33:19,320
At least no one will think you’re crazy.

451
00:33:21,360 --> 00:33:23,520
But I’m stuck having dinner
with a crazy guy like you.

452
00:33:43,880 --> 00:33:45,560
Why don’t you look at the camera?

453
00:33:48,680 --> 00:33:49,600
Just turn a little.

454
00:33:49,600 --> 00:33:51,400
I only need your side profile.

455
00:33:52,680 --> 00:33:53,440
What are you doing?

456
00:33:54,520 --> 00:33:54,800
Come on.

457
00:33:55,600 --> 00:33:59,160
Is it really that hard to
turn your head left and right?

458
00:34:00,680 --> 00:34:01,720
Walking is harder.

459
00:34:06,000 --> 00:34:08,719
Raise your glass a little higher.

460
00:34:12,679 --> 00:34:13,320
Just a little.

461
00:34:16,280 --> 00:34:16,800
Take a sip.

462
00:34:19,960 --> 00:34:20,400
Yes.

463
00:34:39,719 --> 00:34:41,679
One good thing about
hanging out with someone is…

464
00:34:42,800 --> 00:34:44,040
getting a nice photo like this.

465
00:34:44,679 --> 00:34:45,679
You don’t have to take a selfie.

466
00:34:48,120 --> 00:34:49,440
Pun usually takes photos for me.

467
00:34:49,840 --> 00:34:50,120
Yeah?

468
00:34:51,280 --> 00:34:52,280
Why didn’t Pun come with you today?

469
00:34:54,400 --> 00:34:57,680
I made a rule for myself.
I spend my birthday alone.

470
00:34:58,920 --> 00:34:59,240
Why?

471
00:35:03,840 --> 00:35:07,360
Well, your birthday is an important day,

472
00:35:08,960 --> 00:35:12,440
so you should spend it with the
most important person, and that is yourself.

473
00:35:16,520 --> 00:35:19,640
That way, you can talk to yourself,

474
00:35:21,760 --> 00:35:23,000
listen to your own voice,

475
00:35:24,640 --> 00:35:27,000
and cut out unnecessary things in life.

476
00:35:29,040 --> 00:35:29,680
So…

477
00:35:31,040 --> 00:35:32,160
What do you do when it’s time
to blow out the birthday candles?

478
00:35:34,320 --> 00:35:35,360
Just skip that part.

479
00:35:36,480 --> 00:35:39,480
I just said you should
cut out unnecessary things.

480
00:35:41,840 --> 00:35:43,040
No matter how you put it,
that still sounds lonely.

481
00:35:47,720 --> 00:35:49,680
What about your birthday?

482
00:35:50,680 --> 00:35:51,360
My birthday?

483
00:35:52,040 --> 00:35:52,400
Mm.

484
00:35:54,080 --> 00:35:55,080
Same thing every year.

485
00:36:04,000 --> 00:36:06,480
Bottoms up!

486
00:36:08,560 --> 00:36:12,560
Honestly, I barely remember
what happens each year.

487
00:36:16,840 --> 00:36:19,320
Doesn’t that make you feel lonely?

488
00:36:20,600 --> 00:36:21,280
I’m asking seriously.

489
00:36:41,040 --> 00:36:41,720
Well…

490
00:36:44,240 --> 00:36:45,920
I’ll admit, I feel lonely sometimes.

491
00:36:48,960 --> 00:36:50,240
But that’s normal, isn’t it?

492
00:36:52,200 --> 00:36:55,640
In the end, everyone gets lonely.

493
00:36:57,280 --> 00:37:00,080
You just have to learn how to live with it.

494
00:37:05,320 --> 00:37:05,880
That’s true.

495
00:37:18,440 --> 00:37:22,280
♪ Happy birthday, happy birthday ♪

496
00:37:22,560 --> 00:37:26,920
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

497
00:37:28,120 --> 00:37:31,080
This year, try doing something unnecessary.

498
00:37:32,360 --> 00:37:35,000
These three employees
had to bring you a cake.

499
00:37:35,360 --> 00:37:36,600
That’s a lot of work for them.

500
00:37:38,520 --> 00:37:39,520
Make a wish.

501
00:37:40,680 --> 00:37:41,520
Do you know how?

502
00:37:42,640 --> 00:37:43,160
I do.

503
00:37:44,120 --> 00:37:45,400
Happy birthday, Mr. Moth.

504
00:37:47,200 --> 00:37:47,880
Thank you.

505
00:38:07,080 --> 00:38:09,520
One good thing about
celebrating your birthday with someone…

506
00:38:10,240 --> 00:38:11,440
is getting a surprise like this.

507
00:38:28,160 --> 00:38:29,000
Happy birthday.

508
00:38:40,800 --> 00:38:41,480
Should I put it on for you?

509
00:39:12,040 --> 00:39:13,040
For your birthday this year,

510
00:39:13,840 --> 00:39:22,080
I wish you lots and lots of happiness,
and I hope you…

511
00:39:24,520 --> 00:39:27,520
Honestly, I don’t know
what I should wish for you.

512
00:39:28,840 --> 00:39:29,440
I can’t think of anything.

513
00:39:29,440 --> 00:39:33,320
But I’m happy…

514
00:39:36,160 --> 00:39:37,120
we got to know each other.

515
00:40:07,480 --> 00:40:08,520
You’ve got some on your lips.

516
00:40:10,120 --> 00:40:10,360
Huh?

517
00:40:10,640 --> 00:40:11,480
On your lips.

518
00:40:12,360 --> 00:40:12,680
Yeah?

519
00:40:15,720 --> 00:40:16,720
The other side.

520
00:40:16,920 --> 00:40:17,280
Here?

521
00:40:17,600 --> 00:40:18,240
Closer to the middle.

522
00:40:19,120 --> 00:40:19,440
Here?

523
00:41:28,520 --> 00:41:29,800
Is that a surprise from you too?

524
00:41:30,400 --> 00:41:30,800
Yeah.

525
00:41:31,560 --> 00:41:32,080
You like it?

526
00:42:11,480 --> 00:42:12,480
Can you really go home now?

527
00:42:15,160 --> 00:42:16,280
Do you really want me to leave?

528
00:42:20,480 --> 00:42:21,080
I’m kidding.

529
00:42:22,520 --> 00:42:23,360
This is where I say goodbye.

530
00:42:24,040 --> 00:42:24,640
I’m going.

531
00:42:26,040 --> 00:42:26,520
Bye-bye.

532
00:42:44,600 --> 00:42:45,000
Hey.

533
00:42:50,000 --> 00:42:50,840
Do you like me?

534
00:42:58,480 --> 00:42:59,520
So damn much.

535
00:43:13,080 --> 00:43:16,360
- If you truly like me,
go on dates with me for 21 days.

536
00:43:17,080 --> 00:43:18,000
- What do I get if I win?

537
00:43:18,200 --> 00:43:19,320
- Do I get to kiss you again?

538
00:43:20,160 --> 00:43:20,880
- What is this?

539
00:43:21,480 --> 00:43:22,600
- Isn’t it supposed to be just us?

540
00:43:23,840 --> 00:43:26,320
- Dates aren’t supposed to be like this.

541
00:43:26,880 --> 00:43:29,840
- If you guys really don’t click,
why don’t you just step back?

542
00:43:29,960 --> 00:43:30,680
- You can’t!

543
00:43:30,800 --> 00:43:32,440
- Dr. Pun and I haven’t gotten anywhere yet.

544
